andidate uses the wrong QUDT unit IRI, qudt:KiloW (http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/KiloW), instead of the canonical recommended unit http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/KiloW; declare the appropriate unit prefix and use unit:KiloW consistently. It also imposes xsd:decimal numeric-value constraints even though the supplied canonical metadata declares no datatype; remove the guessed datatype requirements and corresponding decimal-only presence/comparison filters unless an authoritative requirement record supplies that datatype. Preserve conditional applicability, ship ownership, inclusive 1000/2800 kW floors, and the prior instruction that comparison logic must not permit an accidental pass across multiple supplied values.","blocking":false,"semantic_attempt_consumed":false}
